From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 22:50:59 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 06/74] Plutonium: shell mode on DRM, evdev input fix,
 display-plane path

- Shell mode (--plutonium-shell-url): the shell page is the only,
  fullscreen window; shelf, tray and notifications hidden.
- Hit test: rewrite EXO-EMBED client-id-0 children before the cycle
  check, so an Exo window whose client id matches the page's isn't
  dropped as a cycle (clicks went to the page instead of the app).
- Exo: an embedded window covering the display gets the fullscreen
  scanout feedback tranche (client picks a scanout-capable modifier).
- Overlays: without an independent cursor plane, skip SingleOnTop and
  Fullscreen proposals that the topmost-scaled rule always blanks, so
  the underlay combination is tested.
- gbm: import formats gbm doesn't report (NV12) with GBM_BO_USE_SCANOUT
  first, so they get a KMS framebuffer.
- Popped-out windows are fitted to the work area.
- Rate-limited EXO-DIAG logging for overlay and hit-test decisions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
